      "writtenOn": "2024-11-01T04:58:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried the Play one. I think they revive because they call [`setProgress`](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/notifications/build-notification#progressbar) to update the progress bar. So they keep sending notifications and replace the old one if there is.\n\nThe announcement is from [here](https://developer.android.com/about/versions/14/behavior-changes-all#ux). There are four exceptions. I guess we don\u0027t fit any of them? But maybe we can just keep updating the notification every 10 minutes or so to actively remind users there is a Vm running and draining your battery.",
      "parentUuid": "3f15a65c_5a384075",
      "revId": "0c2d4654beb81e23f3afa975258f2f4e35ca8dbc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
